<p>{% person "a-benjamin-dove-jr", "A. Benjamin Dove Jr." %}The Reverend A. Benjamin Dove Jr.{% endperson %} became pastor in September 1959. He and his wife, {% person "barbara-dove" %}Barbara{% endperson %}, moved to Mandan from Minnewaukan, North Dakota. Dove served the congregation for more than 30 years. In 1968, Sunday school rooms on the east side of the 1916 building were remodeled as Stark Hall. A new chancel and $25,000 pipe organ were dedicated on May 11, 1969. In 2014, church members renamed and rededicated the Dove Educational Wing in recognition of the Doves' service.</p>
